From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] uiautomationcore: events with arguments, their COM handlers, and the MSAA bridge

UI Automation's events that carry arguments were stubs: the six UiaRaise*
functions for them did nothing, UiaAddEvent refused property changed
events (E_NOTIMPL), and IUIAutomation's Add/Remove handlers for property,
structure, text edit, changes and notification events were E_NOTIMPL. The
MSAA bridge (UiaProviderFromIAccessible) answered most of
ILegacyIAccessibleProvider, SetFocus, ElementProviderFromPoint and the
MSAA WinEvents with E_NOTIMPL. As documented now:

- UiaRaiseAutomationPropertyChangedEvent, UiaRaiseStructureChangedEvent,
  UiaRaiseAsyncContentLoadedEvent, UiaRaiseTextEditTextChangedEvent,
  UiaRaiseNotificationEvent and UiaRaiseChangesEvent raise their events
  with their arguments (E_INVALIDARG without a provider). The arguments
  cross to a listening process as a VARIANT array beside the nodes
  (IWineUiaEvent::raise_event takes them).
- UiaAddEvent takes property changed events for the properties listed,
  and only those reach the callback.
- IUIAutomation: AddPropertyChangedEventHandler(NativeArray),
  AddStructureChangedEventHandler, AddTextEditTextChangedEventHandler
  (for the change type named), AddChangesEventHandler and
  AddNotificationEventHandler, and their Remove calls; each handler gets
  its event's arguments.
- The proxy WinEvent sink adds property and structure changed events.
- MSAA bridge: ILegacyIAccessibleProvider's Name, Value, Description,
  State, Help, KeyboardShortcut, DefaultAction, GetSelection, Select,
  DoDefaultAction and SetValue go to the IAccessible; SetFocus is
  accSelect(SELFLAG_TAKEFOCUS); ElementProviderFromPoint is accHitTest;
  EVENT_OBJECT_NAMECHANGE, VALUECHANGE and HELPCHANGE become property
  changes with the new value, REORDER a children-invalidated structure
  change, SELECTION and INVOKED the ElementSelected and Invoked events;
  UIA_PFIA_UNWRAP_BRIDGE gives back a bridged provider. 11 of Wine's
  uiautomation todos pass.

Not done: the ActiveTextPositionChanged handler (no such event in the
event table yet) and event handler groups.

Gate: test/uiaevents-gate.sh (64- and 32-bit, test/uiaevents-probe.c).
Mutants SG_MUTANT_NO_ARG_EVENTS (uia_event.c), SG_MUTANT_NO_COM_PROP_HANDLER
(uia_com_client.c), SG_MUTANT_NO_LEGACY_ACTION, SG_MUTANT_NO_MSAA_EVENTS
(uia_provider.c).
